WEBVTT

00:01.321 --> 00:04.888
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.898 --> 00:08.177
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.187 --> 00:11.822
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.832 --> 00:14.825
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.835 --> 00:18.195
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.205 --> 00:21.565
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.575 --> 00:23.142
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.152 --> 00:24.796
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.806 --> 00:30.243
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:37.688 --> 00:39.680
Why do you still read the newspaper?

00:39.690 --> 00:40.870
Nobody does that anymore.

00:40.880 --> 00:42.512
I like to keep up on local news.

00:42.522 --> 00:44.070
Like the police blotter.

00:44.080 --> 00:46.657
Huh, most of these arrests
are Cleveland.

00:46.667 --> 00:48.993
And the arresting officer
is Joe Swanson.

00:49.003 --> 00:50.260
Can I help you, sir?

00:50.270 --> 00:52.329
I'm doing my mail route, Joe.

00:52.339 --> 00:54.331
Maybe you'd be more comfortable

00:54.341 --> 00:56.374
talking about it down at the station.

00:56.780 --> 00:58.002
You're right.

00:58.012 --> 00:59.837
<i>It is more comfortable here.</i>

00:59.847 --> 01:01.271
<i>The police station:</i>

01:01.281 --> 01:02.940
<i>come for the racial profiling,</i>

01:02.950 --> 01:04.984
<i>stay for the comfort.</i>

01:08.322 --> 01:10.147
Is that... is that you?

01:10.157 --> 01:13.150
Oh. Yeah. A friend invited me
to this charity ball.

01:13.160 --> 01:15.319
A friend? She's 100!

01:15.329 --> 01:17.321
What are you up to?

01:17.331 --> 01:19.256
Nothing. I enjoy her company.

01:19.266 --> 01:21.425
Older women are cultured, worldly.

01:21.435 --> 01:23.761
I've got nothing to be defensive about.

01:23.771 --> 01:25.162
Her husband passed away.

01:25.172 --> 01:26.330
She appreciates my friendship.

01:26.340 --> 01:27.765
I'm providing companionship.

01:27.775 --> 01:28.999
Dogs are known for that.

01:29.009 --> 01:30.743
I don't like it.

01:38.578 --> 01:40.711
Peter, I need you to mow the lawn.

01:40.721 --> 01:42.046
It's out of control.

01:42.056 --> 01:43.213
I can't mow the lawn, Lois.

01:43.223 --> 01:45.315
The Friends of Distinction
are out there,

01:45.325 --> 01:46.884
grazing in the grass.

01:46.894 --> 01:48.185
♪

01:48.195 --> 01:52.523
<i>It sure is mellow
grazing in the grass</i>

01:52.533 --> 01:55.993
<i>Grazing in the grass is a gas,
baby, can you dig it?</i>

01:56.003 --> 01:59.763
<i>Everything here is so clear,
you can see it</i>

01:59.773 --> 02:03.400
<i>And everything here is
so real, you can feel it</i>

02:05.145 --> 02:07.838
<i>I can dig it, he can dig it,
she can dig it, we can dig it</i>

02:07.848 --> 02:10.741
<i>They can dig it, you can
dig it, oh, let's dig it</i>

02:10.751 --> 02:13.410
<i>Can you dig it, baby?</i>

02:13.420 --> 02:15.179
Oh, let me get in on that!

02:16.523 --> 02:18.162
Where'd they go?

02:21.095 --> 02:23.420
Cleveland? You okay in there?

02:23.430 --> 02:24.588
Cleveland!

02:24.598 --> 02:26.023
Wha-Wha-What? What?

02:26.033 --> 02:28.859
Oh. Yeah, yeah. I'm fine.

02:28.869 --> 02:31.061
Mmm, that was a good toilet dream

02:31.071 --> 02:33.512
about my neighbor and his lawn.

02:33.957 --> 02:35.866
Peter, I don't care who's grazing.

02:35.876 --> 02:37.267
The lawn looks terrible.

02:37.277 --> 02:38.435
Get out there and mow it.

02:38.445 --> 02:40.871
Why can't Chris mow it? He's old enough.

02:40.881 --> 02:42.439
Look, I'm all for Chris mowing the lawn,

02:42.449 --> 02:43.774
but you got to teach him.

02:43.784 --> 02:45.209
Fine, I'll do it tomorrow.

02:45.219 --> 02:47.111
After my weekend job as a zookeeper

02:47.121 --> 02:49.480
with very muscular thighs.

02:49.490 --> 02:51.248
"Thigh" there, nice to see you all.

02:51.258 --> 02:54.251
As you can see right here and here,

02:54.261 --> 02:56.086
I am qualified to be a zookeeper.

02:56.096 --> 02:57.588
This is my friend Frederick.

02:57.598 --> 03:00.023
And I am sure you're all
wondering how much I can squat.

03:00.033 --> 03:02.092
For that answer, you'll have
to go to my Instagram,

03:02.102 --> 03:03.927
YourThighness99.

03:03.937 --> 03:06.263
Now, I'd like to open up
the floor for questions.

03:06.273 --> 03:08.265
- Yes, what food does the bird...
- Not about the bird!

03:08.275 --> 03:10.434
Now, who wants to see me jump
over this fence

03:10.444 --> 03:11.902
from a standing start?

03:11.912 --> 03:15.639
Let me scooch these shorts up
a little "thigher."

03:15.649 --> 03:17.141
Look out, elephants!

03:19.507 --> 03:22.246
So, everybody happy
they went to the zoo?

03:22.256 --> 03:23.814
No?

03:23.824 --> 03:26.383
Well, that's the zoo.

03:35.102 --> 03:38.162
Is that a diamond-encrusted watch fob?

03:38.172 --> 03:39.930
This? Oh, yeah, I-I've had this.

03:39.940 --> 03:42.633
Nobody's owned one of those
for 80 years!

03:42.643 --> 03:45.135
What are you up to?

03:45.145 --> 03:46.637
You already did this.

03:46.647 --> 03:48.205
I'm not trying to show skepticism.

03:48.215 --> 03:49.740
My head is too heavy!

03:49.750 --> 03:53.374
I heard the doctor whisper
to Lois, "3,000th percentile."

03:57.958 --> 04:00.117
Okay, Chris, now, if you're
gonna learn how to mow a lawn,

04:00.127 --> 04:03.187
the first lesson is that
you always start by 7:00 a.m.,

04:03.197 --> 04:06.356
before everyone wakes up,
including roosters.

04:07.801 --> 04:09.459
What the...?

04:09.469 --> 04:10.861
Hey, shut up!

04:10.871 --> 04:12.029
You shut up!

04:12.039 --> 04:14.198
Oh, real original.

04:14.208 --> 04:15.465
Now, to start the mower,

04:15.475 --> 04:17.301
you grab this pull cord like so

04:17.311 --> 04:19.203
and give it a nice hard yank.

04:20.981 --> 04:22.668
Can I change my grip?

04:26.653 --> 04:28.378
Wow, much better.

04:28.388 --> 04:30.314
It's a more familiar motion.

04:30.324 --> 04:34.284
For the rest, you can just watch
this how-to video on YouTube.

04:34.294 --> 04:36.386
What's going on, guys? I'm Corey,

04:36.396 --> 04:38.822
here to take your lawn mowing
skills to the next lev.

04:38.832 --> 04:40.991
But, first, make sure
you subscribe to my channel,

04:41.001 --> 04:42.125
Corey's World.

04:42.135 --> 04:44.027
Okay, now let's start that mower.

04:44.037 --> 04:46.196
Did you know
Corey got recruited by ISIS?

04:46.206 --> 04:49.132
He disappeared, and now there's
this guy doing ISIS videos

04:49.142 --> 04:51.068
and they think it's Corey.

04:51.078 --> 04:52.736
Assalamu alaikum, guys!

04:52.746 --> 04:55.172
This is Corey, here to talk
about making a dirty bomb

04:55.182 --> 04:57.434
with stuff you can find in your kitchen.

05:07.290 --> 05:09.253
Great Caesar's ghost!

05:09.263 --> 05:11.521
<i>Chris and a chubby little friend?</i>

05:11.531 --> 05:14.324
It's like in my dream!

05:14.334 --> 05:15.893
Hey there, Chris.

05:15.903 --> 05:18.428
You know, I've been looking
for a muscley-armed young fella

05:18.438 --> 05:19.630
to mow my lawn.

05:19.640 --> 05:21.064
Sorry, Mr. Herbert,

05:21.074 --> 05:23.066
but I don't even want to mow this lawn.

05:23.076 --> 05:25.736
You could bring your friend
over there to help you.

05:25.746 --> 05:28.238
Come on, Herbert. Rope this calf.

05:28.248 --> 05:31.241
Would $600 a week change your mind?

05:31.251 --> 05:33.810
Uh, would it? You got a deal!

05:33.820 --> 05:36.013
And I can pay you under the table.

05:36.023 --> 05:38.181
I like to make a little fort
under there.

05:38.191 --> 05:41.184
I call it Fort Dix.

05:41.194 --> 05:42.519
Did you hear that, Dad?

05:42.529 --> 05:44.521
He'll pay us $600!

05:44.531 --> 05:47.176
Uh, yeah, did-did you not hear
about Fort Dix?

05:57.110 --> 06:00.637
Oh, Admiral, you've been so good
to me these past weeks,

06:00.647 --> 06:02.239
with my husband gone

06:02.249 --> 06:05.142
and me alone to tend
to his massive estate.

06:05.152 --> 06:07.077
You know, helping you
might have been difficult

06:07.087 --> 06:09.079
were you not so utterly charming.

06:09.089 --> 06:13.083
Oh...

06:13.093 --> 06:15.152
Plus, helping you helps me forget

06:15.162 --> 06:16.253
my own country's troubles

06:16.263 --> 06:18.588
and my struggle to save
our national flower,

06:18.598 --> 06:20.157
<i>the Masdevallia orchid.</i>

06:20.167 --> 06:22.326
That's my favorite flower.

06:22.336 --> 06:24.428
And pet charity.

06:24.438 --> 06:25.829
Really?

06:25.839 --> 06:28.765
I've devoted my life
to raising money to save it.

06:28.775 --> 06:30.100
What a coincidence.

06:30.110 --> 06:31.835
<i>You and the count.</i>

06:31.845 --> 06:34.552
- The count?
- Yes, of Monte Hall.

06:34.863 --> 06:37.140
We like to October in Zurich.

06:37.150 --> 06:39.776
Ah, yes, the best place to October.

06:39.786 --> 06:42.179
The secret, however,
is to October in Zurich

06:42.189 --> 06:45.849
but in September, to avoid
the obnoxious Octobering crowds,

06:45.859 --> 06:48.285
saving October for Paris...
Novembering there...

06:48.295 --> 06:50.287
Then Decembering in Palm Beach
in November

06:50.297 --> 06:52.122
and, in December, Januarying, of course,

06:52.132 --> 06:53.457
as always, in Gstaad.

06:53.467 --> 06:55.525
We December in London.

06:55.535 --> 06:58.362
You, madame, are a cream-faced loon.

06:58.372 --> 07:01.865
Count, I don't believe
you've met the admiral.

07:01.875 --> 07:03.200
Well, he may be an admiral,

07:03.210 --> 07:06.203
<i>but he's certainly not admirable.</i>

07:06.213 --> 07:07.404
Panty drop.

07:07.414 --> 07:08.438
Swoon.

07:08.448 --> 07:09.916
Commercial.

07:18.018 --> 07:21.210
So, Admiral, you must have had
quite the military career.

07:21.220 --> 07:22.852
Your honors are impressive.

07:22.862 --> 07:25.805
Is that medal
a stretched-out carnival penny?

07:25.815 --> 07:27.295
Thank you for noticing, Count.

07:27.305 --> 07:29.251
It means a lot from a man whose top hat

07:29.261 --> 07:31.020
looks suspiciously like an Amazon Echo

07:31.030 --> 07:32.421
with a cardboard brim.

07:32.431 --> 07:34.990
Why, wha-wha-what a preposterous notion!

07:35.000 --> 07:36.481
- Alexa?
- No, don't say that!

07:37.569 --> 07:39.366
What the hell are you doing here?

07:39.376 --> 07:41.397
This is my scam. Now butt out.

07:41.407 --> 07:43.065
Now, why would I do that, Brian?

07:43.075 --> 07:44.466
These old bags are going to die.

07:44.476 --> 07:46.568
Someone's going to end up
with their money.

07:46.578 --> 07:47.770
Look, all right,

07:47.780 --> 07:49.271
there's no reason
to sabotage each other.

07:49.281 --> 07:52.041
There's plenty of Newport
heiresses for the both of us.

07:52.051 --> 07:54.043
Maybe we could even help each other.

07:54.053 --> 07:55.144
Exactly.

07:55.154 --> 07:57.146
Two con men like us working together?

07:57.156 --> 07:58.185
We'll be set.

07:58.195 --> 08:00.582
Like a passive-aggressive alarm clock.

08:00.592 --> 08:02.918
Uh, I don't know if you've noticed,

08:02.928 --> 08:04.687
but the sun's been up
for, like, an hour.

08:04.697 --> 08:06.555
No, no, no, no,
you don't have to get up.

08:06.565 --> 08:07.956
Let your wife do everything.

08:07.966 --> 08:10.125
Just keep sleeping.
You're a good husband.

08:10.135 --> 08:12.628
I'm sure she doesn't fantasize
about your contractor,

08:12.638 --> 08:14.897
who's already downstairs working on...

08:14.907 --> 08:17.466
Well, I can't really figure out
what he's working on.

08:17.476 --> 08:19.815
OH, I KNOW: your wife.

08:24.005 --> 08:25.383
Hey there, Chris!

08:25.385 --> 08:27.042
And what's your pal's name??

08:27.052 --> 08:28.073
I'm Peter, sir.!

08:28.083 --> 08:30.612
You're big for your age,
ain't ya, Petey?

08:30.622 --> 08:33.882
Yeah. Doctor says I eat too much candy.

08:33.892 --> 08:35.651
Ain't no shame in being chubby.

08:35.661 --> 08:37.152
You're a growing boy.

08:37.162 --> 08:39.088
Why, what's this?

08:39.098 --> 08:41.323
Wow! How'd you do that?

08:41.333 --> 08:42.558
It wasn't a trick.

08:42.568 --> 08:43.992
It was stuck to your neck.

08:44.002 --> 08:46.891
Oh, yeah. Sometimes
I fall asleep on candy.

08:53.812 --> 08:55.370
There she is.

08:55.380 --> 08:58.774
The wealthiest heiress
in all of Newport.

08:58.784 --> 09:01.343
- The Holy Grail for guys like us.
- Who is she?

