10:34.701 --> 10:36.104
- Pip?
- Pip.

10:36.114 --> 10:38.407
Been trying to schmooze her for months.

10:38.417 --> 10:40.409
The only catch is
her 95-year-old husband

10:40.419 --> 10:42.544
is still hanging on by a thread.

10:42.554 --> 10:44.213
I can't make a move until he dies,

10:44.223 --> 10:45.714
which, hopefully, is any day now.

10:45.724 --> 10:48.283
If we can charm her,
we'll be set for life.

10:48.293 --> 10:50.118
No more scraping and scavenging,

10:50.128 --> 10:51.954
like a laughing hyena.

10:51.964 --> 10:53.956
I don't sound desperate,

10:53.966 --> 10:55.624
but I'm very desperate.

10:55.634 --> 10:58.994
I'm not a very capable predator.

10:59.004 --> 11:03.098
My family's back
at the den waiting for me.

11:03.108 --> 11:06.702
I think this
is the day I starve to death.

11:06.712 --> 11:09.972
Just kidding, I have no family.

11:09.982 --> 11:13.542
But I'm a very involved uncle.

11:20.092 --> 11:23.185
Dad, shouldn't we attach a bag
to the mower?

11:23.195 --> 11:25.020
That's too much work.
Just mow with the blower

11:25.030 --> 11:27.465
always pointed toward Joe's lawn.

11:31.870 --> 11:34.363
Hey, will you put a bag on that thing?

11:34.373 --> 11:37.032
Just poop into your hand if you have to.

11:37.042 --> 11:38.914
I'll be down in a minute.

11:39.816 --> 11:44.172
Hey, boys. I've got some cookies
and special grape juice for you.

11:44.182 --> 11:46.141
Come on and get it, Petey.

11:46.151 --> 11:47.985
Sweet.

11:50.022 --> 11:53.048
But, Mr. Herbert,
you always made the cookies

11:53.058 --> 11:55.817
with the large pill
in the center for me.

11:55.827 --> 11:58.887
Sorry, Chris. He just got to them first.

11:58.897 --> 12:01.153
<i>I thought I was your favorite.</i>

12:08.974 --> 12:12.200
<i>You mustn't think you've failed me</i>

12:12.210 --> 12:15.837
<i>Just because there's someone else</i>

12:15.847 --> 12:19.141
<i>You were the first real love</i>

12:19.151 --> 12:22.253
<i>I ever had</i>

12:24.256 --> 12:27.249
<i>And all the things I ever said</i>

12:27.259 --> 12:30.886
<i>I swear they still are true</i>

12:30.896 --> 12:33.255
<i>For no one else</i>

12:33.265 --> 12:36.191
<i>Can have the part of me</i>

12:36.201 --> 12:40.595
<i>I gave to you</i>

12:40.605 --> 12:45.000
<i>Torn between two lovers</i>

12:45.010 --> 12:48.737
<i>Feeling like a fool</i>

12:48.747 --> 12:52.007
<i>Loving both of you</i>

12:52.017 --> 12:55.777
<i>Is breaking all the rules</i>

12:55.787 --> 13:00.248
<i>Torn between two lovers</i>

13:00.258 --> 13:03.418
<i>Feeling like a fool</i>

13:03.428 --> 13:08.466
<i>Loving you both
is breaking all the rules.</i>

13:12.437 --> 13:14.963
All right, now let's kick it up a notch.

13:14.973 --> 13:17.666
<i>Come on, shake your body,
baby, do that conga</i>

13:17.676 --> 13:19.901
<i>You know you can't
control yourself any longer.</i>

13:28.353 --> 13:29.644
There she is.

13:29.654 --> 13:31.480
We just got to wait
for our chance to move in.

13:31.490 --> 13:33.015
Brian, look.

13:38.864 --> 13:40.989
You think this might be... the end?

13:40.999 --> 13:43.000
I don't know, but now's our chance.

13:46.238 --> 13:48.139
I hate myself for doing this.

13:50.767 --> 13:54.503
Is that a Cats Protective League
pin on your lapel?

13:54.513 --> 13:56.138
Why, yes.

13:56.148 --> 13:58.440
It's my favorite charity.

13:58.450 --> 14:00.175
I love cats.

14:00.185 --> 14:03.145
I've devoted my life to helping them.

14:03.155 --> 14:04.946
I like this party.

14:04.956 --> 14:06.648
Pussies.

14:06.658 --> 14:08.109
- Cock.
- Cock.

14:08.504 --> 14:12.187
I'm sorry, gentlemen,
but my husband is feeling ill

14:12.197 --> 14:14.189
and stepped into the men's locker room.

14:14.199 --> 14:16.992
Would you be so kind as to check on him?

14:17.002 --> 14:19.039
Well, I'm not sure if we'll be able
to find him.

14:19.049 --> 14:20.731
Don't worry. I've got a very thick,

14:20.741 --> 14:23.434
yellow toenail finder app on my phone.

14:27.145 --> 14:30.138
Ew. Ew. Ew. Ew. Ew.

14:30.148 --> 14:32.107
Ew, ew, ew, ew, ew, ew, ew, ew, ew, ew.

14:32.117 --> 14:33.834
Ew!

14:33.844 --> 14:34.969
Got him.

14:36.165 --> 14:37.571
Do you think he's dead?

14:40.009 --> 14:41.850
Get the hell out of my face, Brian.

14:41.860 --> 14:43.218
Wha... Quagmire?

14:43.228 --> 14:45.353
No. Quagmire!

14:45.363 --> 14:47.556
- That's what I said.
- Oh. Oh, sorry.

14:47.566 --> 14:49.724
I didn't, I didn't hear you
'cause of the prosthetics.

14:49.734 --> 14:52.060
Hey, just checking to see
if the old man is dead.

14:52.070 --> 14:53.262
Oh, hey, guys.

14:53.272 --> 14:55.172
Geez, how many of us are doing this con?

14:55.173 --> 14:58.166
I've got no chance, have I?
A tertiary character like me.

14:58.176 --> 15:00.802
You most certainly do not.
I don't even think

15:00.812 --> 15:02.504
we're going to give you
the dance you rehearsed.

15:12.268 --> 15:14.760
<i>- You're Margaret's husband?
- That's right.</i>

15:14.770 --> 15:16.595
Listen, rookie,
you're out of your league.

15:16.605 --> 15:19.331
You think you know how to bang
a woman who's seen a dodo bird?

15:19.341 --> 15:20.933
Wait, but how can you be married?

15:20.943 --> 15:22.368
You don't even live together.

15:22.378 --> 15:24.303
She's old. She says,
"You weren't here yesterday."

15:24.313 --> 15:26.305
I say, "Yes, I was." And that's it.

15:26.315 --> 15:29.041
Well, you've clearly invested
a lot of time into this.

15:29.051 --> 15:31.810
And yet two fellows like us
with loose lips

15:31.820 --> 15:33.746
could cause it all to fall apart.

15:33.756 --> 15:35.481
- Who's this trombone?
- I'm the guy

15:35.491 --> 15:38.784
who enjoyed like hell
shopping for this little ruse.

15:38.794 --> 15:41.487
Look, there's plenty
of money to go around,

15:41.497 --> 15:43.289
and I don't know how much more
of this I can take,

15:43.299 --> 15:44.890
so I'll make a deal with you guys.

15:44.900 --> 15:46.925
If you can help me "wrap this up,"

15:46.935 --> 15:49.128
if you know what I mean...
Take her skydiving,

15:49.138 --> 15:52.097
something that might, you know,
overwhelm her elderly heart...

15:52.107 --> 15:53.799
I'll split the estate with you two.

15:53.809 --> 15:56.044
But unless you're prepared
to kill her, get the hell out.

15:57.146 --> 15:59.171
All right, I got to run.
It's her birthday.

15:59.181 --> 16:00.839
Happy birthday

16:00.849 --> 16:03.676
Dear Margaret Woolworth
Carrington Von Schumacher

16:03.686 --> 16:06.612
Chanel Astor Livingston
Compte de Saint-Exupery...

16:06.622 --> 16:08.947
I'm, uh, just gonna hang here
for a minute.

16:08.957 --> 16:10.282
Von Trapp Wykenham Hearst

16:10.292 --> 16:12.484
Montgomery Rothchild
Johnson & Johnson

16:12.494 --> 16:14.787
Twillsworth Dolce Gabbana
Von Zweiger

16:14.797 --> 16:17.656
Second Montgomery De LaRoche
Geico Vanderbilt

16:17.666 --> 16:19.158
Lannister Van Buren Butterworth

16:19.168 --> 16:20.292
How I Met Your Mother

16:20.302 --> 16:23.128
Wrigley Louise-Dreyfuss
Ludwig Morgan Stanley

16:23.138 --> 16:25.664
Dumont Lamborghini
Forbes Higbee Winthrop

16:25.674 --> 16:28.367
Chanel Remi Martin
Fitzwilliam Kennedy

16:28.377 --> 16:31.203
Motel Six Fairchild
Brook Pritzker Davenport

16:31.213 --> 16:34.506
Von Stolen Monty Python
Ellisworth Aston Martin

16:34.516 --> 16:37.209
Haverbrook Ziff Lauder Hilton DuPont

16:37.219 --> 16:39.878
Kincaid Winslow Coors
Oviatt Marlborough

16:39.888 --> 16:42.314
Pembroke Huffington
Bush Mellon Sinclair

16:42.324 --> 16:45.317
Mellencamp Starbucks Van Dyke
Third Montgomery

16:45.327 --> 16:47.920
Marriott Barrington Chadsworth
Big League Chew

16:47.930 --> 16:50.189
Chesterfield Kensington Booth Bishop

16:50.199 --> 16:52.791
Longbottom Nottingham
Meisterburger Burgermeister

16:52.801 --> 16:56.362
Tudor Hapsburg
Rockefeller Onassis...

16:56.802 --> 16:57.948
That's a...

16:58.374 --> 17:00.411
that's a freshly oiled hinge.

17:10.015 --> 17:12.420
Petey, let's play horsey.

17:15.524 --> 17:17.249
That's it!

17:17.259 --> 17:21.854
It's time you do all the work
and I goof off with Mr. Herbert.

17:21.864 --> 17:23.422
Like hell it is.

17:30.305 --> 17:33.399
Jesse, is this really happening?

17:33.409 --> 17:35.701
You're going down, old man.

17:35.711 --> 17:38.036
<i>I ain't the one going down.
You're going down.</i>

17:38.046 --> 17:40.572
No way. I'm gonna pound your ass!

17:40.582 --> 17:43.442
You're seeming kind of cocky,.

17:43.452 --> 17:45.043
Boo, cocky!

17:45.053 --> 17:47.012
Oh!

17:52.361 --> 17:55.154
Why are you being such a jerk, Dad?

17:55.164 --> 17:57.689
D-D-D-D-D-Dad?

17:57.699 --> 18:00.192
Yeah, this is my dad.

18:05.707 --> 18:09.368
Well, he often said he wanted
to explode all over me.

18:09.378 --> 18:11.069
He finally did.

18:11.079 --> 18:12.905
Sorry I got jealous, Dad.

18:12.915 --> 18:14.773
That's all right, Chris.

18:14.783 --> 18:17.276
Hey, did you get a little
aroused when we were wrestling?

18:17.286 --> 18:19.253
- No.
- Me, neither.

18:27.429 --> 18:31.423
I am Herbert!

18:33.435 --> 18:35.461
I am Herbert.

18:35.471 --> 18:38.573
I am Herbert. I am Herbert.

18:42.878 --> 18:44.169
Good Quahog, evening.

18:44.179 --> 18:46.171
Uh, let's, uh, let's do that again.

18:46.181 --> 18:49.154
Good evening, Hog-quo,
I'm Tucker Tom. Nope.

18:49.164 --> 18:52.110
Good aftereveningnoon,
HogTom, Quo I'merTuck.

18:52.120 --> 18:53.946
Quo Goodningnoon, TomerTuck,

18:53.956 --> 18:56.348
I'm ningningafterevenQuo, Noonhog.

18:57.793 --> 19:00.352
Newport's wealthiest heiress,
Margaret Woolworth...

19:00.362 --> 19:02.120
Holy God, I'm not reading all that...

19:02.130 --> 19:05.457
Was found dead in her home
of an apparent heart attack.

19:05.467 --> 19:07.793
- Did you...?
- No. Did you?

19:07.803 --> 19:10.529
No. You think Quagmire did?

19:13.742 --> 19:16.301
You, uh... you guys actually did it.

19:16.311 --> 19:18.971
And made it look like a heart attack.

19:18.981 --> 19:21.173
Wow. I, uh...

19:21.183 --> 19:22.941
I didn't think you had it in you.

19:22.951 --> 19:25.711
I... I guess you thought wrong.

19:25.721 --> 19:28.347
Listen, I-I know there's been
some bad blood between us,

19:28.357 --> 19:30.182
but I-I promise, it won't happen again.

19:30.192 --> 19:31.717
I hope you can forgive me.

19:31.727 --> 19:34.620
Well... just watch your step.

19:34.630 --> 19:36.154
Well, a deal's a deal,

19:36.164 --> 19:38.257
so here's your share of the estate.

19:38.267 --> 19:40.268
Just sign here.

19:44.339 --> 19:45.898
- We're rich!
- We're rich!

19:48.443 --> 19:50.035
We're rich, Stewie.

19:50.045 --> 19:52.704
And no flip joke can take that away.

19:52.714 --> 19:55.707
Gentlemen,
due to a disastrous investment

19:55.717 --> 19:58.310
<i>in a Mindy Project amusement park,</i>

19:58.320 --> 20:00.479
Miss Woolworth etcetera, etcetera,

20:00.489 --> 20:03.482
died owing $18 million,

20:03.492 --> 20:05.851
for which you are now liable.

20:05.861 --> 20:07.252
We owe money?

20:07.262 --> 20:09.187
Look, Stewie, it-it could be worse.

20:09.197 --> 20:10.789
We could be dead, like Margaret.

20:10.799 --> 20:12.724
You're right. Poor thing.

20:12.734 --> 20:16.070
I guess she just died of natural causes.

20:19.274 --> 20:21.233
What a couple of rubes.

20:21.243 --> 20:24.570
I'm finally out
from under that crushing debt.

20:24.580 --> 20:27.582
I suppose I don't need this anymore.

20:29.084 --> 20:32.298
Yes, that's right. It was a Meg story.

20:43.539 --> 20:45.664
<i>Come on, shake your body,
baby, do the conga</i>

20:45.674 --> 20:47.733
<i>I know you can't control
yourself any longer</i>

20:47.743 --> 20:49.368
<i>Feel the rhythm of the music
getting stronger</i>

20:49.378 --> 20:50.903
<i>Don't you fight it
till you've tried it</i>

20:50.913 --> 20:52.171
<i>Do the conga beat</i>

20:52.181 --> 20:55.941
<i>Everybody, gather 'round now</i>

20:55.951 --> 20:58.586
<i>Let your body feel the heat...</i>

20:59.548 --> 21:03.049
Thank you for watching "Bob's Burgers " on
www.FOX-fan.tv